{% comment %}
  Care Instructions tab content — @param section {section}
{% endcomment %}

<div class="frido-scg__content">
  <h2>Basic Cleaning Routine for Barefoot Shoes</h2>

  <div class="frido-scg__care-steps">
    {%- liquid
      assign care_steps = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'care_step'
    -%}

    {%- if care_steps.size > 0 -%}
      {%- for block in care_steps -%}
        <article class="frido-scg__care-step" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
            <div class="frido-scg__care-step-media">
              {{
                block.settings.image
                | image_url: width: 600
                | image_tag:
                  loading: 'lazy',
                  widths: '300,400,600',
                  sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 22rem, 100vw',
                  alt: block.settings.title
              }}
            </div>
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="frido-scg__care-step-media">
              {{ 'lifestyle-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder-svg' }}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="frido-scg__care-step-body">
            <h3>{{ block.settings.title | escape }}</h3>
            <div class="rte">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>
          </div>
        </article>
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <article class="frido-scg__care-step">
        <div class="frido-scg__care-step-media">{{ 'lifestyle-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder-svg' }}</div>
        <div class="frido-scg__care-step-body">
          <h3>1. Preparation</h3>
          <p>
            Remove any loose dirt or debris from the shoes. Take out the insoles and laces to clean them
            separately.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="frido-scg__care-step">
        <div class="frido-scg__care-step-media">{{ 'lifestyle-2' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder-svg' }}</div>
        <div class="frido-scg__care-step-body">
          <h3>2. Protective Measures</h3>
          <p>
            Place the shoes, insoles, and laces into a mesh laundry bag to prevent potential damage during
            the wash cycle.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="frido-scg__care-step">
        <div class="frido-scg__care-step-media">{{ 'product-apparel-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder-svg' }}</div>
        <div class="frido-scg__care-step-body">
          <h3>3. Washing Instructions</h3>
          <p><strong>Cycle Selection:</strong> Use the delicate or gentle cycle on your washing machine. This setting minimizes agitation, reducing wear on the shoes.</p>
          <p><strong>Water Temperature:</strong> Opt for cold water to prevent any potential shrinkage or color fading.</p>
          <p><strong>Detergent:</strong> Use a mild, dye-free, and scent-free detergent to maintain the material's integrity and avoid skin irritation.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="frido-scg__care-step">
        <div class="frido-scg__care-step-media">{{ 'product-apparel-2' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder-svg' }}</div>
        <div class="frido-scg__care-step-body">
          <h3>4. Drying Process</h3>
          <p><strong>Air Drying:</strong> After washing, reshape the shoes and allow them to air dry at room temperature. Avoid direct sunlight or heat sources, such as radiators, which can deform or damage the materials.</p>
          <p><strong>Insole and Lace Care:</strong> Ensure insoles and laces are thoroughly dried before reinserting them into the shoes.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <h2>Odor Prevention Tips for Barefoot Shoes</h2>
  <p>
    Since <strong>barefoot shoes</strong> are often made from natural materials, odor buildup can be a common
    issue. Here's how to prevent it:
  </p>
  <ol class="frido-scg__steps">
    <li>
      <strong>Air Out Regularly</strong><br>
      After wearing your barefoot shoes, remove the insoles and let both the shoes and insoles air out
      completely. Placing them in a dry, ventilated area will prevent moisture buildup and keep odors in
      check.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Use Baking Soda</strong><br>
      Sprinkle a little baking soda inside your barefoot shoes after wearing them. Let it sit overnight to
      absorb moisture and neutralize any odors, then shake it out in the morning.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Essential Oils for Freshness</strong><br>
      For a pleasant scent and natural antibacterial properties, add a drop of tea tree or lavender oil to a
      cotton ball and place it inside your shoes overnight. It'll keep your barefoot shoes smelling fresh
      and clean.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    By following these simple cleaning and odor prevention steps, you'll be able to keep your
    <strong>barefoot shoes</strong> in great condition for longer!
  </p>

  <h2>What to Avoid When Cleaning Barefoot Shoes</h2>
  <ol class="frido-scg__steps">
    <li><strong>Hard Scrubbing:</strong> Excessive scrubbing can damage flexible materials.</li>
    <li><strong>Direct Sunlight:</strong> Avoid sun exposure as it can weaken the materials.</li>
    <li><strong>Harsh Detergents or Bleach:</strong> Stick to mild cleansers to prevent material damage.</li>
    <li><strong>Long Soaks:</strong> Avoid soaking, as it may cause mold. Use an anti-mold spray if needed.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Keep Your Shoes Fresh for Every Adventure!</h2>
  <p>
    With this <strong>shoe size guide</strong> and simple tips for <strong>cleaning shoes</strong>, you'll
    keep your barefoot shoes looking great and lasting longer on every journey.
  </p>

  <div class="frido-scg__help">
    <h2>Additional Help</h2>
    <p>
      Need more assistance with finding the right size? Our customer service team is here to help you with
      personalized advice.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>📧</strong>
      <a href="mailto:{{ section.settings.support_email | default: 'hello@frido.com' }}">
        {{- section.settings.support_email | default: 'hello@frido.com' | escape -}}
      </a>
    </p>
    <p>Feel free to reach out with any questions, and happy shopping!</p>
  </div>
</div>
